  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term sea turtle conservation: a key tool for adaptive management and decision making</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will conduct night patrols to survey and protect nesting sea turtles from April 1 - September 30 along 81 km of nesting beaches at Celestun, El Cuyo and Holbox as well as outreach and eduaction activities with local communities. The USFWS will work closely with grantee in setting goals, priorities, and developing budgets, and will provide assistance as needed and requested in engaging with National Governmental and other institutions to improve collaboration and conservation outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
